{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And when men quarrel.</b> I know only men; from where do I derive women? Rabbi Eliezer would say: since laws of damages were stated in the Torah without specification, and the verse specifies for you one of them in which women are treated as men, I generalize all the laws of damages in the Torah to treat women as men." "<b>Or with a stone.</b> As in its Targum: בכורמיזא (with a stone). And so we find in Torat Kohanim regarding וחלצו האבנים: with stones or with כורמזיון, that is, with a stone with which one may die — for if you say it means the fist of a hand, what is the meaning of 'and he does not die'? For would one have expected to die from a blow of the hand?"], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:59:26.024776392Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}